---
import PageLayout from '@layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import SectionLabel from '@components/typography/SectionLabel.astro';
import { contact, site } from '@data/site';

const crumbs = [{ label: 'Terms of Use', href: '/legal/terms' }];
const updated = '17 February 2026';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms governing use of the MMT Impact website, including accuracy of published information, intellectual property and reporting fraudulent use of our identity."
  crumbs={crumbs}
  hero={{
    eyebrow: 'Legal / Terms',
    lines: ['Terms of use.'],
    lede: 'The terms on which this website is provided, and what our published information does and does not constitute.',
    seed: 'terms-hero',
    src: '/images/legal-page/terms-hero.jpg',
    variant: 'graticule',
    size: 'compact',
  }}
  cta={false}
>
  <section class="legal surface-paper section">
    <div class="wrap legal__wrap">
      <aside class="legal__rail">
        <div class="legal__rail-inner">
          <SectionLabel index="—" label="Terms of use" />
          <p class="t-meta legal__updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <div class="prose-editorial legal__body">
        <h2>Accuracy of information</h2>
        <p>
          We take care that information published on this site is accurate at the time of
          publication. Programme information, impact figures, opportunities and vacancies change,
          and we correct or restate published figures when better data becomes available —
          including downward.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where a figure carries a stated basis of reporting, that basis is part of the figure.
          Quoting the number without it misrepresents what we published.
        </p>

        <h2>Not an offer or commitment</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing on this site constitutes an offer, a commitment to fund, to award a contract, or
          to enter a partnership. Registration as a supplier or consultant places an organisation on
          our roster; it does not create an entitlement to be invited to bid or to be awarded work.
        </p>
        <p>
          Programme and project descriptions include work that is in design or planned. Where a
          project is not yet delivering, it is labelled as such, and it should not be read as a
          record of completed delivery.
        </p>

        <h2>The MMT Group</h2>
        <p>
          {site.legalName} is a member of the wider MMT Group. MMT Care, MMT Alliance and MMT Impact
          are separate legal entities. Nothing on this site should be read as MMT Impact holding,
          controlling or being entitled to the assets, turnover, workforce, contracts,
          certifications or delivery history of another Group organisation.
        </p>

        <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          Content on this site is owned by MMT Impact or used with permission. You may quote from it
          with attribution for non-commercial purposes such as research, journalism or academic
          work. Reproducing substantial parts, or using our name, logo or branding, requires written
          permission from <a href={`mailto:${contact.media}`}>{contact.media}</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Photographs of identifiable people are published under specific consent and may not be
          reused, cropped, recaptioned or redistributed under any circumstances.
        </p>

        <h2>Fraudulent use of our identity</h2>
        <p>
          MMT Impact never charges a fee to apply for a role, to register as a supplier or
          consultant, to bid, or to be awarded work. No member of our staff is authorised to request
          a payment or personal benefit in connection with recruitment or procurement.
        </p>
        <p>
          Legitimate correspondence comes from an <strong>mmtimpact.org</strong> address. If you
          receive a request for payment, or contact from a similar-looking domain, do not respond
          and do not send documents or money. Report it to{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${contact.general}`}>{contact.general}</a> or through our{' '}
          <a href="/transparency#whistleblowing">confidential reporting channel</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>External links</h2>
        <p>
          We link to external sites where they are useful. We are not responsible for their content
          or their privacy practices.
        </p>

        <h2>Availability</h2>
        <p>
          We aim to keep this site available and secure but do not guarantee uninterrupted access.
          We may change or withdraw content at any time.
        </p>

        <h2>Accessibility</h2>
        <p>
          This site targets WCAG 2.2 AA. If you encounter a barrier to using it, tell us at{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${contact.general}`}>{contact.general}</a> and we will fix it and, where
          you need the information sooner, provide it in another format.
        </p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of South Sudan. Nothing in them
          limits any right you have that cannot be limited by law.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${contact.general}`}>{contact.general}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .legal__wrap {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .legal__wrap {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.45fr) minmax(0, 1.55fr);
    }
    .legal__rail-inner {
      position: sticky;
      top: calc(var(--header-height, 104px) + 2rem);
    }
  }

  .legal__updated {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }
</style>
